# Copy to .env (git-ignored). Only EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables are readable by the app, and anything
# prefixed that way is shipped inside the app bundle. NEVER put an API key here; the Anthropic
# key belongs on the server (apps/server/.env).

# Where the app finds the backend. In development you can leave this unset: the app derives the
# address from the Expo dev server's host (so phones on the same Wi-Fi just work) and assumes
# port 3000. Set it explicitly for emulators that can't reach the host or for production.
#   Android emulator -> http://10.0.2.2:3000
#   Production       -> https://your-api.example.com   (must be HTTPS)
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=
